 ## check.sh
 
-### §check-fails-open — the check never blocks a commit because of its own failure
+### §check-fails-closed — an internal failure aborts the check with a non-zero exit
+- Since: 2026-10-22
+- Decision: `set -euo pipefail`. Any failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit. Large staged files are
+  still only a warning (`exit 0`).
+- Supersedes: §check-fails-open, by maintainer decision.
+- Reason: failing open hid the check's own breakage; nobody found out when something inside it broke.
+- Note: under `-e`, conditional output in the file loop must use `if …; then …; fi`, not `[ … ] && …`. A false test as
+  the loop's last command makes the pipeline fail and aborts on every ordinary commit.
+
+### §check-fails-open — SUPERSEDED 2026-10-22 by §check-fails-closed
 - Since: 2026-09-11
 - Decision: `set -uo pipefail` without `-e`. Every internal error still ends in `exit 0`; the script only warns.
 - Forbidden: `set -e` or `set -o errexit`, and any exit status other than 0.
